---
import CookbookShell from './CookbookShell.astro';
import { BOOK_METADATA } from '../../data/cookbook/book-metadata';
---

<CookbookShell title={`Copyright & Disclaimer | BiblicalMeal Cookbook`}>
  <section class="cookbook-content px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-24">
    <h1 class="font-display text-h1 text-ink">Copyright &amp; Disclaimer</h1>

    <div class="prose-bm mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-6 text-body text-ink-muted">
      <p>{BOOK_METADATA.copyright}</p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-h3 text-ink">Recipe Classification</h2>
      <p>
        Every recipe in this cookbook is classified according to its evidence
        basis. Recipes labelled <em>Scripture-inspired</em> are modern creations using
        ingredients attested in the biblical world. Recipes labelled <em
          >Reconstruction</em
        > are scholarly best-effort assemblies based on historical evidence. Recipes
        labelled
        <em>Historically-Informed</em> preserve the distinction between attested food
        concepts and modern practical formulas. No recipe in this cookbook claims
        to represent an exact ancient preparation unless explicitly stated and supported
        by cited evidence.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-h3 text-ink">Historical Evidence</h2>
      <p>
        Historical claims in this cookbook are traceable to cited research.
        Where evidence is uncertain, inference is distinguished from direct
        attestation. Archaeological claims reference specific finds and
        scholarly sources. No historical claim is presented as certain unless
        the evidence supports that level of confidence.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-h3 text-ink">Scripture</h2>
      <p>
        Scripture quotations follow the King James Version (KJV). All references
        cite book, chapter, and verse. Scripture text is quoted carefully and
        claims do not extend beyond the recorded text.
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-h3 text-ink">Modern Adaptations</h2>
      <p>
        Modern cooking quantities, methods, equipment, and ingredients are
        identified as practical adaptations. These are modern kitchen choices
        that honour the ancient tradition without claiming to replicate specific
        historical preparations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</CookbookShell>
